"""Approximate vowel-ending spelling continuations across token boundaries.

Short continuations starting c/k/q (and corresponding letters or kana) are
positive after a vowel, especially e. Longer fragments are weaker. After e,
continuations beginning with b/v/s/u tend to have the opposite sign. This is
an orthographic approximation, not a pronunciation or word-meaning analysis.
