inline code span in prose (the "`" before `path` in "made to the file at `path`"), and
moderately negative on opening quotation marks such as “ 「 《. It is near zero almost
everywhere else. Closing backticks, glued to punctuation or a newline, are weaker.

The program reads only the current token and a short look-back (LOOKBACK tokens):
  - a single backtick with no backtick in the look-back (the first after prose) is -4 to -5;
