"""Approximate a current-token item/entry vocabulary detector.

Training examples show large negative responses to item and items, both as
ordinary nouns and as code names. Singular item is stronger. Case and glued
punctuation adjust the strength; longer compound names are attenuated.
Related nouns, iteration names, and selected multilingual goods/counting
words get weaker responses. Everything else is zero. This deliberately
omits history-dependent variation and diffuse, small token-specific effects.
